meta {
 name Razomy Notation
 version 0.3.0
 extension ".rn"
 type Md
 tags (
  ONTOLOGICAL-DATA
  RL-ISOMORPHIC-LAYER-0
  TYPE-AGNOSTIC-CORE
  TYPE-CONSTRUCTORS
  SYMMETRIC-PENTAD
  ADAPTIVE-INDENT-QUANTUM
  AUTO-CLOSED-DELIMITERS
  UNIFIED-NONE


part FORMAL VOCABULARY (THE 7 ORTHOGONAL CONCEPTS)

Every construct in Razomy Notation (`.rn`) and Razomy Language (`.rl`) is derived from seven orthogonal concepts:

vocabulary (
 Concept, Syntax, Ontological Definition
 1. Node, `Key Value`, The universal AST unit: a `Key` (left of space) bound to a `Value` (right of space).
 2. Key, `id` / `a.b` / `'sym` / `"str"`, The variable, field, or tag identifier (`snake_case` by convention). Can carry attached metadata `Key{Props}(Slots)`.
 3. Value, `Type? Pentad` | `Scalar`, The payload assigned to a `Key` (either one of the 5 Pentad structures or an atomic Scalar).
 4. Type, `Md` / `Sql` / `Date` / `Uuid`, A `PascalCase` archetype. Attached with NO space (`Sql(`, `Html[`, `Scss{`, `Date"`), it acts as a **Type Constructor** that parses/validates the inner structure.
 5. Pentad, `[` `{` `(` `"` `#`, The 5 structural delimiters: `[` Stream, `{` Form, `(` Tuple, `"` Raw, and `#` Comment.
 6. Scalar, `None` / `true` / `42` / `'pk`, Atomic literals inside `{` and `(`: `None`, `Bool`, `Num`, `Sym`, `Str`.
 7. Algebra, `&` / `^` / `/`, Space-surrounded operators between `Key` and `Value` for merging (`&`), symmetric difference (`^`), and key stripping (`/`).


part AXIOMATIC SPECIFICATION (LAYER 0 — DEDUCTIVE HIERARCHY)

section AXIOM I: THE STREAM ROOT & ROOT TYPE BINDING

Razomy Notation (`.rn`) is an ontological data and markup notation that serves as the isomorphic Layer 0 substrate of the Razomy Language (`.rl`).

ul [
 b[Universal Stream Root] — Every `.rn` file begins as an implicit Stream `[` at indentation level 0. Free text, outliner trees, markup nodes, and structured data blocks (`config {`) coexist in a single continuum right from line 1.
 b[Type-Agnostic Core vs. Type Constructors] — The `.rn` core parser has zero hardcoded domain keywords. Compound file extensions (`*.md.rn`, `*.json.rn`, `*.rl`) or inline Type Constructors (`Md[`, `Sql(`, `Html[`, `Scss{`, `Json"`) bind a `PascalCase` Type to the AST subtree (for example, the `Md` type interprets `title`, `part`, `section`, `topic` lines as document headings).


section AXIOM II: SPATIAL TOPOLOGY (ONE LAW FOR `[`, `{`, `(`, `#`)

All structural delimiters (`[`, `{`, `(`, `#`) obey one universal topological law — explicit closing tokens at the end of a line or block are NEVER required:

topic 1. Inline Mode (Same-Line Payload -> Auto-Close at EOL)
If content follows `[`, `{`, `(`, or `#` on the same line, it is an Inline construct:
ul [
 b[EOL Auto-Closure] — Reaching the end of the line (`\n`) automatically closes any open inline `[`, `{`, `(`, or `#`:
  `h1 [ Why Razomy?`
  `env { NODE_ENV production, PORT 8080`
  `cmd (node, server.js`
  `# Inline homoiconic comment auto-closed at EOL`
 b[Mid-Line Explicit Closure] — A closing `]`, `}`, or `)` is only required when another token or comma follows on the SAME line: `Read b[this] now`, `pt (10, 20), { a 1 }`.
 b[Separators] — Inside inline `{` and `(`, elements are separated by `,`. Inside `[` and `#`, content is continuous text flow.

topic 2. Block Mode (End-of-Line Open -> Dedent Auto-Close)
If `[`, `{`, `(`, or `#` (or a Type Constructor `Type[`, `Type{`, `Type(`) is the LAST token on a line, it opens an indented block:
ul [
 b[Adaptive Indent Quantum (`Q = 1, 2, or 4`)] — The canonical indentation quantum is **1 space** (`Q = 1`). However, the parser dynamically detects `Q` (`1`, `2`, or `4` spaces) from the environment/file's first indented line, requiring `+Q` spaces per nesting depth thereafter.
 b[Dedent Auto-Closure] — Dedenting on a non-blank line automatically closes all blocks (`[`, `{`, `(`, `#`) deeper than the new indentation level. Explicit closing brackets and trailing commas are NEVER used in block mode.
 b[Blank-Line Invariance] — Blank lines never trigger a dedent; they are ignored inside `{` and `(`, and act as paragraph separators inside `Md[` and `#` blocks.
 b[Dot-Path Flattening (`a.b.c`)] — A dotted key `a.b.c {` unfolds into `{ a { b { c { ... } } } }` while requiring only a SINGLE `+Q` indent on the next line.


section AXIOM III: THE SYMMETRIC PENTAD (`[` STREAM, `{` FORM, `(` TUPLE, `"` RAW, `#` COMMENT)

Every non-scalar structure in `.rn` belongs to one of five symmetric modes, any of which can be constructed by attaching a `PascalCase` Type with NO space (`Type[`, `Type{`, `Type(`, `Type"`, `Type#`):

topic 1. `[` Stream Mode (Sequential Flow, Outliner, Markup & Pipelines)
Represents an ordered continuum of text, markup, or operations. Empty `[]` = empty stream.
ul [
 b[Lines & Paragraphs] — In a raw Stream `[`, each plain line is a distinct item. Under the `Md` type (`*.md.rn` or `Md[`), consecutive plain lines merge into paragraphs, and flat prefix lines (`title`, `part`, `section`, `topic`, `quote`) are interpreted by `Md` as structural headings/blocks.
 b[Outliner Recursion] — Indenting (`+Q` spaces) beneath a plain text line implicitly nests a child Stream `[` under that line.
 b[Inline Nodes & Escaping] — Inside text flow, `Key[` or `Key{Props}(Slots)[` (with NO space before `{`, `(`, or `[`) is parsed as an inline node (`b[bold]`, `a(/docs)[links]`). Literal brackets are escaped via backticks `` `arr[0]` ``, quotes `"[raw]"`, or backslash (`\[`).

topic 2. `{` Form Mode (Key-Value Map / Object / Type Archetype)
Maps `Key Value` statements separated by `\n` (block) or `,` (inline). Empty `{}` = empty form.
ul [
 b[Case-Aware Empty Key Duality] — Inside a `snake_case` (data/instance) Form, a bare `Key` with no payload evaluates to `None`. Inside a `PascalCase` (Type Archetype) Form in `.rl`, a bare `snake_case` `Key` defines an open generic slot `Key _T`.

topic 3. `(` Tuple Mode (1D Lists & 2D Relational Tables)
Represents positional sequences or relational tables. Empty `()` = empty tuple.
ul [
 b[1D List] — Inline `(a, b, c` OR a block `(` where the first indented line contains NO top-level commas (one item per line; items with literal commas are quoted `"Hello, world!"`).
 b[2D Relational Table] — A block `(` where the first indented line contains at least one top-level comma defining the header columns (`col,` for 1 column). Subsequent lines are comma-separated rows mapped to those headers (empty cells `, ,` evaluate to `None`).

topic 4. `"` Raw Mode (Inline Quoted & Column-0 Multiline Strings)
ul [
 b[Inline Quoted (`"..."`)] — Same-line UTF-8 string supporting `\"`, `\\`, `\n`, `\t`, `\{`, and `{expr}` interpolation in `.rl`.
 b[Column-0 Multiline (`(Type)?(N)?"`)] — An opening `"` at the end of a line (`"`, `Ts"`, `Sh"`, `Sql"`, `1"`, `Rn2"`) suspends indentation until a matching `"(N)?` (`"`, `"1`, `"2`) placed strictly alone at Column 0. Every leading space inside is 100% literal, with zero escape processing.
 b[Case-Flexible Formatter Normalization] — Canonical Type constructors are `PascalCase` (`Json"`, `Ts"`, `Sql(`, including user-defined types). If a user writes lowercase `json"` or `ts"`, the parser accepts it and the formatter normalizes it to `Json"` / `Ts"`.

topic 5. `#` Comment Mode (Inline & Block Homoiconic Documentation)
Obeys the exact same Inline vs. Block topological rule as `[`, `{`, `(`:
ul [
 b[Inline Comment (`# text`)] — A `# ` (hash followed by space) outside quotes starts a comment that auto-closes at `\n` and attaches to the AST node. Unspaced tokens like `#42` or `#111111` are literal scalars.
 b[Block Comment (`#` at EOL)] — A bare `#` at the end of a line opens an indented multiline comment block (`+Q` spaces) that automatically closes on dedent — requiring zero `#` prefixes on inner lines and zero closing tokens!


section AXIOM IV: LEXICON & UNIFIED `None`

topic Scalar Auto-Typing (inside `{` and `(`)
lexicon_table (
 Token Pattern, Examples, Ontological Type & Semantics
 Boolean, `true` / `false`, `Bool`
 Unified None, `None` / bare key / `, ,`, `None` (the single universal absence value; serializes to `null` in JSON/SQL)
 Numeric, `8080` / `-3.14` / `0xFF` / `1e-5`, `Int` / `Float` / `Byte` (multi-dot `0.1.0` falls back to String)
 Symbol, `'pk` / `'not_null` / `'GET`, O(1) interned tag (no closing quote; serializes to `"pk"` in JSON)
 Type Constructor, `Date"2026-03-30"` / `Point(10, 20` / `User{id 1`, `PascalCase` Type attached directly to `"`, `(`, `{`, `[` with NO space
 Unquoted String, `postgres` / `/app` / `8px` / `#111111`, Any raw text after `Key ` up to `\n` (in block `{`) or `,` (in `(` / inline `{`)
 Quoted String, `"Hello, world!"` / `""` / `".btn"`, Inline escaped string or Column-0 multiline block


section AXIOM V: THE SPACE LAW (KEY vs. TYPE CONSTRUCTOR) & ALGEBRA

Every statement in `.rn` and `.rl` obeys a strict, unambiguous separation between **Key/Variable** (left of space) and **Value/Constructor** (right of space):

code 1"
Node  ::= Key({Props})?((Slots))? (Algebra)* (" " Value)?
Value ::= (Type)? ( "[" ... | "{" ... | "(" ... | "\"" ... | "#" ... ) | Scalar
"1

ul [
 b[The Space Law (`Key Value` vs. `Type{`)] — A space separates a variable/field name from its value, whereas a Type Constructor attaches directly to its delimiter with **NO space**:
  `env { A 1` — key `env` assigned an untyped Form `{`
  `styles Scss{` — key `styles` assigned a `Scss`-constructed Form `Scss{`
  `query Sql(` — key `query` assigned a `Sql`-constructed Tuple `Sql(`
  `view Html[` — key `view` assigned an `Html`-constructed Stream `Html[`
  `code Ts"` — key `code` assigned a `Ts`-constructed Raw string `Ts"`
  `created_at Date"12.12.23"` — key `created_at` assigned a `Date`-constructed literal
 b[Algebraic Inheritance (` & `, ` ^ `, ` / `)] — Space-surrounded operators combine Forms or Types before the value:
  `Target & Source {` — Deep-merges all fields from `Source` (Identifier, Type, or Dot-Path) into `Target` left-to-right (` MyObject & Object {`). Omitting `{` clones the value directly (`backup_timeout & base.timeout`).
  `Target ^ Source {` — Symmetric difference (retains only keys present in `Target` or `Source`, but not both).
  `Target & Source / key {` — Strips `key` (identifier, `'symbol`, or dotted `a.b`) from the inherited Form (`Target & Source / k1 / k2 {`).


part CANONICAL EXAMPLES (VERIFYING EVERY AXIOM)

section 1. PLAIN TEXT, OUTLINER & BLOCK COMMENTS (Axiom I & III)
example {
 input Rn"
#
 Multiline block comment!
 Indented by +Q space, auto-closed on dedent.
how my day?
 good
todo list # inline comment
 a
 b
 c
"
 output Json"
[
  { "text": "how my day?", "children": ["good"] },
  { "text": "todo list", "children": ["a", "b", "c"] }
]
"

section 2. MARKDOWN DOCUMENT (`*.md.rn` — `Md` Type, Auto-Close & `Ts"`)
example {
 input Rn2"
title Razomy Guide

Fast b[zero-noise] rn a(/docs)[links], with span{class highlight}[inline] tags and `arr[0]` code.

ul [
 No closing tags
 Adaptive 1, 2, or 4 space indentation

benchmarks (
 Format, Tokens, Notes
 JSON,   140,    "Verbose, requires quotes"
 RN,     48,     "Ultra-compact, lean parser"

code Ts"
const x = 42;
function hello() {
  return x;
}
"
"2
 output Md"
# Razomy Guide

Fast **zero-noise** rn [links](/docs), with <span class="highlight">inline</span> tags and `arr[0]` code.

- No closing tags
- Adaptive 1, 2, or 4 space indentation

| Format | Tokens | Notes                      |
| ------ | ------ | -------------------------- |
| JSON   | 140    | Verbose, requires quotes   |
| RN     | 48     | Ultra-compact, lean parser |

```ts
const x = 42;
function hello() {
  return x;
}
```
"

section 3. HTML DOM TREE (Axiom II & V — Attached `{Props}` + Auto-Closed `[`)
example {
 input Rn"
article{id post, class featured, lang en} [
 h1 [ Why Razomy?
 p [ Read the a{href /docs, target _blank}[documentation].
"
 output Html"
<article id="post" class="featured" lang="en">
  <h1>Why Razomy?</h1>
  <p>Read the <a href="/docs" target="_blank">documentation</a>.</p>
</article>
"

section 4. JSON / YAML CONFIG (Axiom II & IV — Dot-Path, `None` & Col-0 Strings)
example {
 input Rn2"
cluster.primary.database {
 engine postgres
 port 5432
 created_at Date"12.12.23"
 token
 fallback None
 empty_str ""
 extra_tags ()
 welcome_msg 1"
Line 1 starts at Column 0 (zero ambiguity with parent indentation!).
  Line 2 has exactly 2 leading spaces of actual text content.
"1
 steps [
  Check replication lag
  Promote primary node
"2
 output Json"
{
  "cluster": {
    "primary": {
      "database": {
        "engine": "postgres",
        "port": 5432,
        "created_at": "12.12.23",
        "token": null,
        "fallback": null,
        "empty_str": "",
        "extra_tags": [],
        "welcome_msg": "Line 1 starts at Column 0 (zero ambiguity with parent indentation!).\n  Line 2 has exactly 2 leading spaces of actual text content.",
        "steps": [
          "Check replication lag",
          "Promote primary node"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
"

section 5. RELATIONAL SCHEMA & TABULAR DATA (2D Tuple, `'symbol` & `None`)
example {
 input Rn"
users_schema (
 column, type, constraint, default
 id,     Uuid, 'pk,        gen_uuid
 org_id, Uuid, Orgs.id,    None
 role,   Text, 'not_null,  member

users_rows (
 id,  org_id, role,   created_at
 u_1, o_10,   admin,  Date"12.12.23"
 u_2, ,       member, Date"13.12.23"
"
 output Sql"
CREATE TABLE users (
  id     UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_uuid(),
  org_id UUID REFERENCES Orgs(id) DEFAULT NULL,
  role   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'member'
);
INSERT INTO users (id, org_id, role, created_at) VALUES
  ('u_1', 'o_10', 'admin', '12.12.23'),
  ('u_2', NULL, 'member', '13.12.23');
"

section 6. CSS / SCSS STYLES (Auto-Closed Inline `(` & `{`)
example {
 input Rn"
".btn" {
 background-color #111111
 padding (8px, 16px
 "&:hover" { background-color #222222
"
 output Scss"
.btn {
  background-color: #111111;
  padding: 8px 16px;
  &:hover {
    background-color: #222222;
  }
}
"

section 7. DOCKER & TERRAFORM INFRASTRUCTURE (Auto-Closed Inline + `Sh1"`)
example {
 input Rn2"
container {
 from node:22-alpine
 workdir /app
 copy (., /app
 run Sh1"
npm ci --omit=dev
"1
 env { NODE_ENV production, PORT 8080
 cmd (node, server.js

resource.aws_s3_bucket.logs {
 bucket my-corp-logs
 acl private
 lifecycle_rule.expiration {
  enabled true
  days 90
"2
 output Tf"
# Dockerfile:
FROM node:22-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY . /app
RUN npm ci --omit=dev
ENV NODE_ENV=production PORT=8080
CMD ["node", "server.js"]

# Terraform (.tf):
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "logs" {
  bucket = "my-corp-logs"
  acl    = "private"
  lifecycle_rule {
    expiration {
      enabled = true
      days    = 90
    }
  }
}
"

section 8. ALGEBRAIC INHERITANCE (Axiom V — `&` Merge & `/` Strip)
example {
 input Rn"
mesh {
 ingress {
  to (auth, api
  protocol grpc
  tls true
 base { timeout 30, retries 3, debug true
 prod & base / debug {
  replicas 5
 backup_timeout & base.timeout
"
 output Json"
{
  "mesh": {
    "ingress": { "to": ["auth", "api"], "protocol": "grpc", "tls": true },
    "base":    { "timeout": 30, "retries": 3, "debug": true },
    "prod":    { "timeout": 30, "retries": 3, "replicas": 5 },
    "backup_timeout": 30
  }
}
"

section 9. MULTI-TYPE COMPONENT CONSTRUCTORS (Attached `Sql(`, `Html[`, `Scss{`)
example {
 input Rn"
UserCard {
 props {
  id Uuid
  theme dark

 query Sql(
  select, from,  where
  "*",    users, "id = :id"

 view Html[
  div{class card} [
   h2 [ User Profile
   p [ Welcome back!

 styles Scss{
  ".card" {
   background-color #111111
   "&:hover" { background-color #222222
"
 output Json"
{
  "UserCard": {
    "props": { "id": "Uuid", "theme": "dark" },
    "query": "SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = :id;",
    "view": "<div class=\"card\"><h2>User Profile</h2><p>Welcome back!</p></div>",
    "styles": ".card { background-color: #111111; }\n.card:hover { background-color: #222222; }"
  }
}
"

section 10. JSON SCHEMA & UI FORM ARCHETYPE
example {
 input Rn"
# 1. Define the Schema / UI Form Type (PascalCase)
UserForm {
 username Str(3, 20){label "Username", pattern "^[a-z0-9_]+$"}
 email    Email{label "Work Email", placeholder "name@company.com"}
 age      Int(18, 120){label "Age", default 25}
 role     Enum('admin, 'editor, 'viewer){label "Role", default 'viewer, widget 'radio}
 bio      Str(0, 500){label "Bio", widget 'textarea, default None}
 tags     List(Str){min_items 1, max_items 5, unique true}
 address {
  city    Str{label "City"}
  zip     Str(5, 10){default None}

# 2. Instantiate & Validate Data against UserForm
valid_user UserForm{
 username alex_razomy
 email    alex@razomy.org
 role     'admin
 tags     (rust, ontology, rn
 address  { city Kyiv
"
 output Json"
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "UserForm",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["username", "email", "tags", "address"],
  "properties": {
    "username": { "type": "string", "minLength": 3, "maxLength": 20, "pattern": "^[a-z0-9_]+$", "title": "Username" },
    "email":    { "type": "string", "format": "email", "title": "Work Email", "placeholder": "name@company.com" },
    "age":      { "type": "integer", "minimum": 18, "maximum": 120, "default": 25, "title": "Age" },
    "role":     { "type": "string", "enum": ["admin", "editor", "viewer"], "default": "viewer", "title": "Role", "ui:widget": "radio" },
    "bio":      { "type": ["string", "null"], "minLength": 0, "maxLength": 500, "default": null, "title": "Bio", "ui:widget": "textarea" },
    "tags":     { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" }, "minItems": 1, "maxItems": 5, "uniqueItems": true },
    "address": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["city"],
      "properties": {
        "city": { "type": "string", "title": "City" },
        "zip":  { "type": ["string", "null"], "minLength": 5, "maxLength": 10, "default": null }
      }
    }
  }
}
"